    {
      "id": "claim_96c84e176b0346b5ad1ae0d75d1b8d55",
      "statement": "Cell states: resident (active or idle); idle cells are removed from memory; hibernated cells keep their hibernatable WebSocket clients on the node; inactive cells exist only as bucket objects (how every cell starts); no memory survives transitions, so the constructor runs again on the next event, and a hibernated cell wakes the same way a cold start does except its clients stay connected and it stays on its node.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L20-L29",
