      "id": "claim_1f8400d77cd54d349590d84f0be2d2ce",
      "statement": "WebSockets become their own tasks because a socket outlives the request that opened it, with three shapes — a local socket to a cell on this node, a socket proxied to the owning peer, and a socket the worker opened outbound — differing only in what sits on the far end.",
