    {
      "id": "claim_8cc8807164cd41659bf3057a7afb1598",
      "statement": "Each hibernatable WebSocket client holds state in the isolate heap, so the V8 heap limit decides how many clients a cell can carry (approximately 50,000 at the 128 MB default, approximately 512 MB for 100,000); above 90% of the limit an isolate refuses a new hibernatable socket and also stops SQL result-set materialization, resuming under 90%, and celld forces a collection when a measurement is above 75%.",
